{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic","id":782835,"title":"Upcoming Requiem Books topic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T08:52:50-08:00","id":782835,"title":"Upcoming Requiem Books topic","content":"I thought we could get a discussion going on about the new, second edition supplements coming out for Vampire. All of it is pretty exciting stuff, so it would be nice to show the devs how hyped up we are and to discuss what we are most excited about in the hopes of perhaps getting a few spoilers (maybe, pretty please?).<br /> <br /> Just in case anyone's missed it, the upcoming supplements are:<ul><li>A Thousand Years of Night (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Secrets of the Covenants (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Half-Damned (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Guide to the Night (Summer 2016)</li> </ul><br /> I'll start. The book I'm most excited about is <i>A Thousand Years of Night</i>. While Ancient Mysteries was a pretty solid addition to Requiem 1e, I felt it was lacking <i>something</i>. It gave us advanced powers to create something powerful and terrifying, but the fluff and fiction of Requiem always seemed to promise more than the mechanics could deliver. I am very excited for the Elder-as-Conspiracy concept, and also about this bit from the release schedule: <i>&quot;This book explores vampires who transcend history&quot;</i>. Also, as Methuselahs are described as vampires who have lived for more than a millennium, and although I believe Methuselahs will not be given a full treatment in the book, the title seems promising in shedding some light as to how does it feel for an Elder that is approaching that thousand years turning point, which is the end of one path and the beginning of the next one.<br /> <br /> Also, as Secrets of the Covenants has been teased the most, it would be nice to get some juicy tidbits from this supplement as well.<br /> <br /> <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>, from the Open Dev docs that we've seen, seems like a great addition. The mechanics are very intriguing and will likely become a staple around most Vampire tables. There's not much more to say, other than that I hope the fiction parts of the book will deliver the same atmosphere as the clanbooks did, and finally solidify how covenants interact with one another across a variety of cities and domains. Also, now that the focus is more global, it would be nice to see how exactly the covenants handle cross-domain interaction and coordination of effort. Do the Invictus <i>really</i> hold award ceremonies for <i>Best Earl of 2015</i>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While I love the idea of more choices for playable characters, <i>Half-Damned</i> loses out (in my opinion) simply because the competition is just too darn good. Still, it will be a great addition that will help flesh out core elements of Requiem's world teased in the corebook, so that's also a certain purchase for me!<br /> <br /> Finally, we have <i>Guide to the Night</i>. A Player's and Storyteller's Guide for Requiem second edition, do I need to say more? Really want to see how Tier Three chronicles can be set up, especially in a way less disruptive to the main game than the Conspiracies of the Danse Macabre supplement. Also, a common theme me and my players enjoy is moving up the Tiers, starting as neonates some centuries ago, becoming ancillae and then finally, becoming movers and shakers of the WoD as powerful elders, so suggestions in handling that transition would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:50:03-08:00","id":782877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic#post782835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we could get a discussion going on about the new, second edition supplements coming out for Vampire. All of it is pretty exciting stuff, so it would be nice to show the devs how hyped up we are and to discuss what we are most excited about in the hopes of perhaps getting a few spoilers (maybe, pretty please?).<br /> <br /> Just in case anyone's missed it, the upcoming supplements are:<ul><li>A Thousand Years of Night (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Secrets of the Covenants (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Half-Damned (Fall 2015)</li> <li>Guide to the Night (Summer 2016)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>They better hustle since we are half way through november. I know astronomically it isn't winter yet but most people I know consider november certainly late November the beginning of winter.<br /> I could use the half damned now. I really want to see how the up the Ghouls( I like blades familiars) and Ghoul families.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:53:52-08:00","id":782880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=782877#post782877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> we are half way through november.</div> </div> </div> </div>...It's December.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:52:54-08:00","id":782922,"title":"","content":"I pretty much have to echo your own preferences, stylanski. I'm really looking forward to an in-depth look at elders and a clanbook-style view of the covenants with a glimpse at Belial's Brood 2.0. Revenants, dhampirs and other half-damned just don't pique any interest in me. And I'm sure the Guide to the Night will have a lot of cool stuff in it.<br /> <br /> Really, though, whatever it is I'll be happy for any supplement for Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2015, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T11:34:45-08:00","id":782954,"title":"","content":"I'm most interested in the Half-Damned book, but the other three are tied for a close second. I <i>love </i>dhampirs, and in fact, my first foray into this industry as a professional was writing a dhampir-related supplement for <i>Unhallowed Metropolis</i>. I'm definitely looking forward to what's coming for <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T11:48:32-08:00","id":782961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=782880#post782880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It's December.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's probably in a different time zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:08:59-08:00","id":782975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=782961#post782961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's probably in a different time zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like a paralel world, I don't think anywhere there's 9 whole days of difference in time zones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:34:47-08:00","id":783006,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking, I think <i>Guide to Night </i>is the one I want the most. Looking at it strategically, that's the one that seems like it'll be most useful for actually running games. S<i>ecrets of the Covenant</i> and <i>A Thousand Years of Night</i> are useful for the same reason.<br /> <br /> I can't wait for <i>Half-Damned</i> either, so I like all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T13:36:44-08:00","id":783035,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping Thousand Years of Night goes less for VtM's &quot;a really, really old asshole&quot; and more of Requiem for Rome's web content that implied they were truly alien creatures. I also like the chance to have a generational game, or a running antagonist for a Mummy chronicle.<br /> <br /> Secrets of the Covenants got my money the second they hinted at more info on the Montreal setting.<br /> <br /> Half-Damned doesn't interest me whatsoever.<br /> <br /> I didn't even know Guide to the Night was happening, but Danse Macabre is my favorite VtR book and a decent contender for favorite nWoD book period. Fingers crossed for more writing of that caliber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T14:39:30-08:00","id":783057,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants is my most hyped release, especially after seeing those teases of Sanctum rituals. I love the idea of fatsplats in place of slim paperback splat books. Between that, the core, and Damnation City, I think I'd have all the materials I could ever want to run a VtR game.<br /> <br /> That said, Guide to the Night is enticing too. I don't really know anything about it, but I've heard nothing but good things abit Danse Macabre, and thus sounds like the spiritual successor to that.<br /> <br /> Thousand Years of Night is intriguing, though I'm not sure how much use I'll have for it, and the premise of Half-Damned just leaves me cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:10:28-08:00","id":783075,"title":"","content":"I want them all, but I have a soft spot for the demi-splats of second edition as I think they are exceptionally well made and bring a lot of color and storyhooks to the respective settings, so maybe if I have to chose only one I would take Half-Dammned in a heartbeat. Thousands Years of Night goes into, for the most part, previously uncharted territory, so it is a close second. Both Secrets of the Covenants and Guide to the Night could prove priceless to me as a Storyteller too, so they share an honorable third position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T16:48:47-08:00","id":783126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783035#post783035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping Thousand Years of Night goes less for VtM's &quot;a really, really old asshole&quot; and more of Requiem for Rome's web content that implied they were truly alien creatures. I also like the chance to have a generational game, or a running antagonist for a Mummy chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these are hopes a lot of us have had for a while. A generational game in Vampire just makes sense. Also, though I would like elders to remain an integral part of the Danse Macabre and active in the All Night Society, I'd love to see Methuselahs as that alien creature that has transcended humanity in such a way that even other Vampires would feel uncomfortable interacting with. How do you react to being related, by blood, to such an entity? For some reason, I imagine most such interactions resembling talks with and quests by Hermaeus Mora from Skyrim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:40:25-08:00","id":783237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783126#post783126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of these are hopes a lot of us have had for a while. A generational game in Vampire just makes sense. Also, though I would like elders to remain an integral part of the Danse Macabre and active in the All Night Society, I'd love to see Methuselahs as that alien creature that has transcended humanity in such a way that even other Vampires would feel uncomfortable interacting with. How do you react to being related, by blood, to such an entity? For some reason, I imagine most such interactions resembling talks with and quests by Hermaeus Mora from Skyrim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anybody know if Thousands usada of night will be out before january?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T22:44:10-08:00","id":783251,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty excited for all of them from a fluff perspective. Covenants mostly, I suppose, since that's the most practical for the typical campaign.<br /> <br /> That said, the previews have left me a little concerned that we'll get power creep in merits and the like. It's a typical problem with RPG supplements. Of course, they're just previews, so it might not be so bad upon release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T06:23:13-08:00","id":783407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783237#post783237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know if Thousands usada of night will be out before january?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Monday Meetings and Publishing Schedule it's not even done with a first draft, so outside of some misdirection it seems very, very unlikely that it will get written, edited, art crafted, presented to Paradox for approval, approved and sent to Drivethru before January.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T06:54:56-08:00","id":783417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783251#post783251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty excited for all of them from a fluff perspective. Covenants mostly, I suppose, since that's the most practical for the typical campaign.<br /> <br /> That said, the previews have left me a little concerned that we'll get power creep in merits and the like. It's a typical problem with RPG supplements. Of course, they're just previews, so it might not be so bad upon release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm less concerned about power creep and more concerned about <i>cool creep</i>. Where the core book is relatively down-to-earth compared to all of the subsequent releases.<br /> <br /> That &quot;Build a vampire frankenstein&quot; Circle of the Crone ritual for instance. <i>Super cool</i>. Way bigger than any of the rituals in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T06:56:52-08:00","id":783418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783407#post783407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the Monday Meetings and Publishing Schedule it's not even done with a first draft, so outside of some misdirection it seems very, very unlikely that it will get written, edited, art crafted, presented to Paradox for approval, approved and sent to Drivethru before January.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you. is paradox the new company owner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:08:29-08:00","id":783422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783418#post783418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you. is paradox the new company owner?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. It looks as if Secrets of the Covenants is going to be the next one out, as it's in editing. It doesn't seem to be in art direction, though, so it may take a few more months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T14:55:04-08:00","id":783678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div cl