opped theball then,cause it sair Thousands years would be out by 2015</div> </div> </div> </div>It should definitely be changed around. It also suggests the second editions of Mage, Promethean and Changeling are coming out in December, as well as Dark Eras and Half-Damned. To be fair it does warn at the top that the times listed indicate intent, and not a guarantee. But I doubt its their intent to rush these products before the month is over while the Changeling 20th Anniversary Kickstarter is going on.<br /> <br /> Going by the Monday Meeting updates offers a better view of the progress things are taking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-10-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T16:50:03-08:00","id":783754,"title":"","content":"The schedules are not concrete, and for that reason. It's just a fact of the industry that things take longer than optimism suggests, books change during the development phase, sometimes drastically, and few people can sustain a living off of roleplaying games alone. Thus, other life commitments often get in the way and hamper progress. When you look at it from a perspective of what actually gets done despite the general difficulties of working in this industry, it's pretty impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:21:35-08:00","id":783814,"title":"","content":"I've always just regarded the deadlines as loose goals. If it results in a higher quality product, I'm fine waiting a few months longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:54:44-08:00","id":783831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/782835-upcoming-requiem-books-topic?p=783678#post783678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think whoever organized e onyx path scheduled dropped theball then,cause it sair Thousands years would be out by 2015</div> </div> </div> </div>As Claire pointed out. You also get used to it after 10+ years of delayed schedules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","val